[b]Expanded co-op for Find The Needle Demo[/b]

Build and expand a shared factory with additional transport machines, overhead building controls, revised progression and targeted synchronization fixes. Current release: 0.19.6-xRangerDE.70, checked against Steam demo build 25963876. All participants must install the same mod and game versions.

[b]Included features[/b]
[list]
[*]Up to eight players including the host. Shared world, buildings, research, purchases and money, with personal tool inventories. The host simulates production and confirms inventory transfers.[/*]
[*][b]Loading hopper:[/b] 10,000 starting capacity, upgrades to 100,000, and output portions from 100 to 1,000 within your unlocked belt limit. Existing 50,000-capacity hoppers keep their capacity and contents. Fill it from above, by robotic arm, with M while using the vacuum, or by right-clicking with carried raw hay/tools. Unaccepted overflow stays in its source. Connect raw-hay belts at the left, rear or right input, start a belt at the front output, or insert the hopper into a straight, level conveyor. Capacity upgrades preserve the on/off state. Dismantling a filled hopper drops its stored hay and needles.[/*]
[*][b]4-, 6- and 8-port mergers and splitters.[/b] Separate paid 4 → 6 → 8 unlock chains; free placement or insertion into a straight, level belt. Empty devices allow input/output selection with E. Arms can link directly to these devices without an intermediate belt.[/*]
[*][b]Overhead building camera:[/b] F7, then B to choose a part. Pan, zoom, place, and hover a machine to open its settings with E. Pan across the entire playable terrain, with a wider zoom range. Hall roofs including extensions and the stand canopy are hidden in overhead view, with selection and building beneath them. The host validates map boundaries and placement; the former 24 m limit around the player no longer applies in overhead view.[/*]
[*]Building controls: tap R for stepped rotation, hold R and move the mouse for free rotation, F6 to reverse a belt after placing its first point, F9 for parallel placement beside angled conveyors and connected bends. Draw long runs in one operation; the mod creates connected native sections at the same per-metre cost. Native connection and collision checks still apply.[/*]
[*]Improved wall/platform and roof alignment, with charcoal, cream, red and green wall/window/door variants using native materials.[/*]
[*]Movable empty sale stations, plus four paid unlocks for up to five stations total. Extra compact scales cost 500 and use the shared prices/account. Aim at an empty station and press N to open its placement preview directly. If N is already assigned, the native hint bar shows a free alternative. After confirmed pickup, carry the station away from its old location. Right-click cancels; E opens settings. Hold X to dismantle extra scales, and toggle the feed belt in the settings of an empty scale.[/*]
[*]20 sale-price ranks, up to twice the base price. Rebalanced upgrade budgets, larger belt portions, expanded arm/lift/stairs/router progression and a purchasable double jump. Existing purchased levels are retained. Recorded overpayments for repriced upgrades are credited once when an older save is loaded.[/*]
[*]Prestige map changes from the delivery board after the physical haystack is empty AND all six needle types are collected. Preview the settlement; retain tools, unlocks and upgrades while buildings and saleable goods are converted to money.[/*]
[*]Host-confirmed needle/scanner transfers, machine-setting synchronization, arm-load and income display replication, and targeted press, wrapper, lift, water-connection and tool-drop fixes.[/*]
[*]Guest vacuum recovery for a process crash and rejoin to the same host world, using a private local journal. Earlier host-save rollback and unsaved host progress are not recoverable by this feature.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Latest update: revision 70[/b]
Move Supply Co with N; its interaction and delivery points follow the saved, synchronized location. The command stays out of the build catalog. Sale-station and shop previews remain visible at close range. Each overhead viewport now receives distant machine animations and loose straw. A small translucent game/mod version label appears at the bottom right.

Arm Spacing offers ten ranks down to 50% required spacing (150,000 total). Arm Carry Size retains eight ranks up to +64% (80,000 total). The complete vacuum budget is 500,000: 300,000 capacity and 200,000 suction. Existing ranks are preserved. Merger surfaces carry the player toward the configured output, and parallel-belt previews follow the adjacent run.

Robot-arm destination search took about 70% less time in a 32-arm native headless benchmark with identical results. This is a targeted CPU improvement, not a rendered FPS claim. Concurrent building, upgrades, editing and rejoining were checked with up to eight local game processes, including packet loss and duplication.

[b]Previous update: revision 67[/b]
Angled and curved parallel conveyors, long conveyor runs in one placement, overhead roof cutaways, confirmed sale-station transport and preservation of mod/add-on unlocks after switching language. Existing collision and host checks remain active.

[b]Previous update: revision 66[/b]
Map-wide overhead building, direct sale-station relocation and translated action hints. New building, hopper, routing, sale and colour labels cover all 17 language options in the current game. Missing core alerts and German-only errors are corrected. Known system messages received from the host are displayed in the recipient’s language. Older untranslated descriptions use English; not every legacy text is translated into all 17 languages.

[b]Previous update: revisions 63–65[/b]
Saving and autosaving work with the updated game. Custom 4/6/8-port devices are restored before world loading, and building controls, native-style panels, transparent icons and hopper connections have been revised. If devices disappeared and the world was saved again, restore a backup that still contains them; removed records cannot be reconstructed.

[b]Installation[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Close the game. Back up your saves and existing mod files.[/*]
[*]Extract the main ZIP. Copy its mods folder into the game directory beside FindTheNeedle.exe. Replace the previous multiplayer folder when updating; do not load two versions together.[/*]
[*]In override.cfg, keep your existing settings and add the following entry under [autoload]:[/*]
[/list]
[code][autoload]
MPMod="*mods/multiplayer/mp.gd"[/code]
If [autoload] already exists, add only the MPMod line. Avoid duplicate entries and a filename ending in .txt.
[list=1]
[*]Start the Steam demo. The host creates the lobby and loads the save; friends join using Steam invitations. Everyone needs the same mod version and a compatible game build.[/*]
[/list]
Updating does not edit your save files. In-game changes and any eligible one-time credit are retained when the host saves. Do not downgrade a save containing new machines without a compatible backup. Never share mp_settings.cfg, recovery journals, saves or diagnostic logs with your installation package.

