[b]Grouped development history[/b]
These are summaries of existing maintenance revisions, not additional downloads you must install. The main file is cumulative; withdrawn builds are not recommended.
[list]
[*]Revisions 1–9: early authority, personal-tool, purchase and conveyor-state corrections; preservation of loose hay and settled item updates.[/*]
[*]10–19: diagnostics, machine intake and drone handling, integrated M-key unloading and lift display work. Revisions 11/12 were withdrawn or superseded; later builds replaced those approaches.[/*]
[*]20–29: routing settings, pipe/power links, press/wrapper buffers, conveyor rebuild safety and lift/stair cargo preservation; V62 compatibility.[/*]
[*]30–39: purchase placement, authoritative selling, stale callback protection, technology/drone replication, world-load lifecycle and arm/cargo displays.[/*]
[*]40–49: water links, optional mouse replication, expanded vacuum upgrades, scanner identity handling, buffered hopper, overhead view, double jump and prestige.[/*]
[*]50–59: save/recovery corrections, personal-tool and loose-hay fixes, revised economy with one-time credits, reduced unchanged-field synchronization work, guest vacuum journal, hopper settings and native-style merger models/insertion.[/*]
[*]60–62: paid 4/6/8-port machines, improved hopper surfaces and accessory placement, direct arm routes, right-click hopper transfers, sale stations, free rotation, belt reversal/parallel mode and house alignment/colors.[/*]
[*]63–65: custom-device save/load restoration, R/F6/F9 input corrections, mouse-capture recovery, all-port direction hints and native-style panels, transparent catalog icons, three hopper inputs and front output, filled-hopper dismantling and belt insertion, sale-scale controls, and compatibility fixes for saving and the hay press after the game update.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Revision 66[/b]
Overhead camera and validated building actions across the playable map; N for direct sale-station relocation with the active key shown in the native HUD; cancel/finish behaviour; wider translation coverage and recipient-language system notifications.

[b]Compatibility and testing limits[/b]
Targets the Windows Steam demo; release 0.19.6-xRangerDE.70 was checked against Steam build 25963876. The core additions work in single-player as well as co-op where applicable. Native local headless tests cover host/guest transactions, packet loss/duplication, save state, mixed cargo and blocked-output recovery. These checks do not establish a two-PC Internet/Steam result, GPU frame rates, compatibility with every mod, or freedom from all bugs. The reported overhead-camera slowdown was not reproduced as a sustained CPU regression in headless profiling; GPU performance remains unverified. The native game and mods can change; back up saves before updating.

For a report, include the game/mod versions, host or guest role, steps to reproduce, and the relevant local diagnostic excerpt with personal data removed. The full per-version history is in CHANGELOG.md inside the ZIP and on GitHub.
